    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106-a8">

                <pb facs="0186" n="104" xml:id="pg104"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#center">[Telegram.—<placeName>Lisbon</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-02-04">February 4,
                        1865</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Hon. H. S. Sanford, United States Minister,
                        Brussels:</hi></p>
                <p>Inform Commodore Craven that several vessels, reported to be rebel cruisers, are
                    hereabouts, and, unless restricted by orders, his services are urgently
                    needed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES E. HARVEY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
